---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Print a scheduler configuration that runs a monitor

Usage: rustman monitor schedule-recipe [OPTIONS] --for <SCHEDULER> <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>
          The monitor (its name)

Options:
      --for <SCHEDULER>
          The scheduler to configure
          
          [possible values: cron, systemd, launchd, github-actions]

      --write <PATH>
          Write the configuration to this file instead of printing it

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
